{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nThe roadmap's timeline starts two days before the earliest span of any item, so one old item stretches the visible range far into the past; the default zoom (week, one cell per day) then shows only a slice of what matters.\n\n## Spec\n\n1. **`projects-roadmap { start \"<offset>\"; zoom \"month\" | \"week\" | \"day\" }`** — a top-level node. `start` is relative to today (`\"-7d\"`, `\"-1m\"`, `\"0d\"`; the current behaviour is the default when absent); items starting earlier are clipped on the left and reachable with `h`. `zoom` is the initial scale (default `week`).\n2. **Per view** — the same `roadmap { … }` child inside a `projects-view` overrides the top-level one for that view.\n3. Docs (Config Reference en / ja with CI-verified examples, the Projects chapter), the Projects demo tape.\n\nRelated: hiding done items (#185) already shrinks the range in most boards; this issue covers the remaining cases.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:39:07Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":187,"state":"OPEN","title":"Projects: configurable roadmap range and default zoom"}
